'''Betakkuma''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] added in [[Version 7.2 Update|Version 7.2]] that can be acquired as a treasure drop when playing any stage of [[Betakkuma Collaboration Event|Groove Like A Bear]] during the [[Betakkuma Collaboration Event]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 432
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Betakkuma
|name2 = Black Betakkuma
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Black Betakkuma''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Although this unit has a low chance to knockback [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] enemies, it is spammable, so it works quite well in stacks, being able to infinitely knock back [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] if RNG favours you well. Treat him as though he were a spammable meatshield with a chance of knocking back Alien enemies, unfortunately this only works on a select few Alien enemies' due to Bettakuma's short range.

As a meatshield, Betakkuma is underwhelming and costly, as his cost of 150¢ is threatening to your [[Worker Cat]] considering his spammabilty. Between his inability to tank hits and everything else, it would be better to just use [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], and their [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|variants]], as they have more survivability than him.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield}}

